/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  furfural -- the vapour pressure of furfural, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 and C283).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate vp
  furfural`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION,
  committed before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to EVERY
  usable laboratory's measurements of it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1021/acs.jced.7b00574         19 pts  326.05-415.15 K  Zheng; Luo; Yin; Chen et al.
      10.1021/je060406c                16 pts  276.7-323.4 K  Emel'yanenko; Dabrowska; Verevkin; Hertel et al.
      10.1021/je020117y                 9 pts  339.16-429.5 K  Fele; Grilc
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      10.1016/j.fluid.2014.10.037: 3 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1016/j.jct.2018.03.019: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/acs.jced.8b00451: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/je400885z: 4 pressure point(s), fewer than 5

  FIT AND GRADED ACCEPTANCE (DEV.md 4c C285, Vitor 2026-11-10; the evidence,
  objective and outliers of C283; declared before the fit).
  EVIDENCE: every study above is fitted; none is held out (C283 amended:
  laboratories disagree with each other by more than they claim, so the
  test is agreement across all of them, not one laboratory's claimed
  precision).  OBJECTIVE: `objective { method twoStage; }` -- least
  squares in log10 P for a first estimate, then the LARGEST relative error in
  P, (P_model - P)/P, over the kept points minimised from it (Vitor's
  practice, C280); both answers kept.  OUTLIERS: after the least-squares
  stage a point with a relative P error above 15 % (three times
  the acceptance) is DISCARDED BY NAME (its study DOI, T and P), listed in
  the result and the record, and the fit repeated without it, once
  (`outliers { maxRelativeError 15 percent; }`).  ACCEPTANCE,
  GRADED, the DEFAULT of C285: the maximum relative P error over all kept
  points is graded clean up to 5 %, warning up to
  10 %, severe up to 20 % and refused above; where the
  normal-boiling-point condition below applies, the absolute gap is graded
  clean up to 1 K, warning up to 2 K, severe up to
  4 K and refused above.  The fit's grade is the WORSE of the
  two.  A clean, warning or severe fit is ACCEPTED and promoted (autoPromoted,
  humanReviewed false) with `fitGrade <grade>;` and the deciding numbers in
  its provenance entry, which the component loader voices on every run that
  uses it (a warning or a severe grade); a refused one is not promoted.  This
  case declares no `system/curationDict`, so the default applies; a case
  that needs another acceptance declares it there, with its reason.  The
  AmbroseWalton curve's errors on the same points are reported beside the
  fit's, as information.

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 434.85 K is judged against the range of the KEPT points (all studies span 276.7-429.5 K before any outlier is discarded): if Tb lies OUTSIDE that range, the fitted Antoine's own normal boiling point (P = 101.325 kPa) is GRADED by its absolute gap to it (the temperature limits of the acceptance below); inside it, the gap is reported and is not a condition.

  EARLIER FITS, SUPERSEDED BY THIS DECLARATION
  @@EARLIER-BEGIN@@
  C281 step 2, objective leastSquares (log10 P), the same partition and
  band: WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 3.638107 - 1181.7414/(T + -109.8817),
  in-sample R2 0.999802 over 19 points, 326.05-415.15 K. HELD OUT: 16
  points, AAD 10.8740 % against the band 5.6 % -> notValidated. Its own
  normal boiling point (101.325 kPa): 435.22 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out
  verdict notValidated (AAD 10.87 % against the band 5.6 % declared
  before the fit); the record keeps AmbroseWalton THEN C281 step 3,
  objective twoStage, one study fitted and one held out, judged by the
  band (superseded by C283): WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`;
  measured, not argued). Objective twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) =
  3.762609 - 1251.4515/(T + -102.1178), in-sample R2 0.999771 over 19
  points, 326.05-415.15 K. HELD OUT: 16 points, AAD 8.1701 % (max 25.1514
  %) against the band 5.6 % -> notValidated; the stage-1 least-squares
  answer on the same points: AAD 10.8740 %, max 31.7748 %. Its own normal
  boiling point (101.325 kPa): 435.23 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out verdict
  notValidated (AAD 8.17 % against the band 5.6 % declared before the
  fit); the record keeps AmbroseWalton. THEN C283, every usable study
  fitted and none held out, accepted only at max relative error <= 5 %
  and Tnb within 1 K (superseded by the graded acceptance of C285): WHAT
  THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued). Objective
  twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 4.578554 - 1695.1936/(T +
  -61.6013), in-sample R2 0.999783 over 44 kept points, 276.7-429.5 K
  (10.1021/acs.jced.7b00574 19/19 kept; 10.1021/je060406c 16/16 kept;
  10.1021/je020117y 9/9 kept). Relative error in P over the kept points:
  mean 2.2435 %, max 5.0725 %; AmbroseWalton on the same points: mean
  4.2916 %, max 9.3434 %. Outliers discarded: none. Its own normal
  boiling point (101.325 kPa): 432.31 K. NOT PROMOTED by the DEFAULT
  acceptance of DEV.md 4c C283 (no system/curationDict): 3 studies, 44
  points kept, 0 discarded as outliers; max relative error 5.073 % (mean
  2.243 %) against 5 %; AmbroseWalton on the same points mean 4.292 % /
  max 9.343 %; the record keeps AmbroseWalton
  @@EARLIER-END@@

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares every
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Objective twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 4.578554 - 1695.1936/(T +
  -61.6013), in-sample R2 0.999783 over 44 kept points, 276.7-429.5 K
  (10.1021/acs.jced.7b00574 19/19 kept; 10.1021/je060406c 16/16 kept;
  10.1021/je020117y 9/9 kept). Relative error in P over the kept points:
  mean 2.2435 %, max 5.0725 %; AmbroseWalton on the same points: mean
  4.2916 %, max 9.3434 %. Outliers discarded: none. Its own normal
  boiling point (101.325 kPa): 432.31 K. PROMOTED on 2026-11-10 into
  data/standards/components/furfural.dat as reviewStatus autoPromoted,
  humanReviewed false, because: fit grade severe under the DEFAULT graded
  acceptance of DEV.md 4c C285 (no system/curationDict), 3 studies, 44
  points kept, 0 discarded as outliers; max relative error 5.073 % (mean
  2.243 %), grade warning (limits 5 / 10 / 20 %); Tb outside the kept
  points' range, normal boiling point 432.31 K, -2.54 K from the record's
  Tb 434.85 K, grade severe (limits 1 / 2 / 4 K); AmbroseWalton on the
  same points mean 4.292 % / max 9.343 %
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  furfural;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/furfural-vapourPressure-acs.jced.7b00574.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/acs.jced.7b00574"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/furfural-vapourPressure-je060406c.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je060406c"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/furfural-vapourPressure-je020117y.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je020117y"; }
                role      fit;
            }
        );

        objective  { method twoStage; }
        outliers   { maxRelativeError 15 percent; }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
